{title: When He Was On The Cross}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Oh, I'm not on an ego trip
I'm [A]nothing on my own
[Em]I make mistakes, ob[A]viously
[G]Common flesh and [D]bones
But I'll prove someday, just what I say
[D]I'm of a special [G]kind
Cause when [A]He was on the cross
[Em]I was [A]on His [D]mind

{comment: Chorus}
[A]Oh, He [D]knew me, yet He [G]loved me
[A]He who bore my pain
Made the heavens [D]cry[A]
So un[D]worthy, of such [G]mercy
Cause when [A]He was on the cross
[Em]I was [A]on His [D]mind

{comment: Verse 2}
The [D]look of love was on His face
[A]Thorns were on His head[Em]
Blood was on [A]His scarlet robe
[G]Stained a crimson [D]red
Though His eyes were on the crowd[D]
He looked ahead in [G]time
Oh, when [A]He was on the cross
[Em]I was [A]on His [D]mind
